@startuml
title RuleSphere - Activity Diagram\n04. Shadow and Canary Rollout | UC-15..17
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #F0ECFF
skinparam activityBorderColor #496477

|Release Manager|
|Control / Delivery Plane|
|Consumer Application|
|Runtime Engine|
|Shadow Worker|
|Authorized User / Analyst|

' Activity 1: Rollout Configuration
|Release Manager|
start
:Configure Shadow and/or Canary settings for candidate;
|Control / Delivery Plane|
:Authorize rollout command and verify candidate eligibility;
if (Authorized and eligible?) then (yes)
  :Distribute artifact and rollout configuration;
  :Notify active Runtime nodes (see Activity 05);
  :Return rollout confirmation;
else (no)
  :Return access / release policy error;
endif
stop

' Activity 2: Production Request & Asynchronous Shadow Execution
|Consumer Application|
start
:Submit unpinned production evaluation request;
|Runtime Engine|
:Authorize runtime scope and resolve routing context;
if (Request admitted?) then (yes)
  :Apply deterministic sticky percentage / cohort policy;
  if (Selected for Canary?) then (yes)
    :Bind eligible loaded Canary snapshot;
  else (no)
    :Bind node-local loaded Active snapshot;
  endif
  if (Bound snapshot available?) then (yes)
    :Validate input and evaluate selected snapshot (see Diagram 06);
    :Return production response to consumer;
    |Consumer Application|
    :Receive production decision;
    |Runtime Engine|
    if (Shadow enabled and mirrored traffic eligible?) then (yes)
      :Dispatch async mirrored request;
      |Shadow Worker|
      if (Production request executed Canary?) then (yes)
        :Evaluate Active snapshot on mirrored input for baseline;
      else (no)
        :Use captured Active outcome as baseline;
      endif
      :Evaluate approved Shadow snapshot on mirrored input;
      :Protect sensitive fields (mask/tokenize);
      if (Both outcomes valid and protection succeeded?) then (yes)
        :Persist correlated protected Active/Shadow diff;
      else (no)
        :Record comparison error without impacting production;
      endif
      stop
    else (no)
    endif
  else (no)
    :Return explicit runtime availability error;
  endif
else (no)
  :Return protocol-appropriate error;
endif
stop

' Activity 3: Query Diff Analysis
|Authorized User / Analyst|
start
:Submit query for Shadow comparison diffs;
|Control / Delivery Plane|
:Authorize query scope;
if (Authorized?) then (yes)
  :Fetch protected diff records from store;
  :Assemble divergence metrics and node reports;
  :Return diff analysis report;
else (no)
  :Return access denied error;
endif
stop

legend bottom
  F-14 Resolution: Rollout configuration, production evaluation, and diff querying are decoupled.
  Shadow processing is dispatched asynchronously without blocking or mutating the production response.
  Canary uses deterministic sticky hash or approved cohort routing.
endlegend
@enduml
